course: dictionary
lesson: 16029
title: Venting feelings and venting air
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Venting has two meanings, and the words around it tell you which one the writer means. In the first, venting means letting out strong feelings, such as anger or frustration, by talking or shouting about them. «After the match, Sam vented his anger to his best friend.» Sam is not hurting anyone. He is letting the feeling out safely.
explain: In the second meaning, venting means letting air, gas, smoke or steam escape through an opening. «The kettle was venting steam from its spout.» Nobody is talking or feeling anything here. Something is simply escaping through a gap.
explain: To pick the right meaning, ask yourself: is this a person's feeling, or is something moving out through a hole? Look for clues such as «anger», «about» or «steam» to decide.
fact: «Venting» means letting out strong feelings, especially anger or frustration, by talking or shouting about them.
fact: «Venting» also means letting air, gas, smoke or steam escape through an opening.
fact: Phrases to know: venting about something, venting anger, venting steam.
fact: Talking to a friend is one safe way of venting your feelings.
fact: The verb forms are vent, vents, vented and venting.
exercise: «She vented her frustration by talking to her sister about the test.» What is venting here? | Closing a window | Breathing in fresh air | Letting steam out of a kettle | *Letting out strong feelings by talking
exercise: «The pipe was venting steam into the cold air.» What is the pipe doing? | Making a loud noise and then stopping | Shouting at the workers | Storing water for later | *Letting steam escape through an opening
exercise: «Ben vented his anger after losing the game.» Find and copy one word that shows the feeling being let out. | *anger | game | Ben | after
test: «The factory vented smoke through its tall chimneys.» What does venting mean here? | Feeling sad about the work | *Letting smoke escape through an opening | Shouting about the factory | Cleaning the chimneys
test: «Mia vents about her busy week to her mum every evening.» What does vents mean here? | *Talks about her feelings to let them out | Closes the door on her week | Blows air into a balloon | Runs round the park
exam: «When Jake is upset, he vents to his friend instead of shouting.» Which option best describes what venting means here? | Opening a window to let in fresh air | *Letting feelings out safely by talking | Breaking something in anger | Keeping every feeling hidden inside
